  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is constrained to move along with a moveable pulley of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;which is connected to a spring of force constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>,&nbsp;as shown in the figure. If the mass of the fixed pulley is negligible and friction is absent everywhere, then the period of small oscillations of the system is<br />\r<u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0059_52edc4df3d39.jpg\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 257px;\" /></strong></u></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mtext>k</mtext></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
